{
  "format": "sfxgen/1",
  "name": "Force field hum (loop)",
  "description": "Standing close to a containment field across a doorway, a seamless loop. The field's emitters hum low, with a hollow, mostly odd set of harmonics that reach up into a rasping edge, slowly breathing through a phaser as the field ripples. Its metal frame sings faintly along. Over the hum the surface of the field fizzes like a power line in rain, a hiss chopped at twice the hum's frequency. Somewhere inside, an unstable current wanders and flips (a gritty buzzing that never repeats), and now and then dust touches the field and pops.",
